e2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "s `\"fee_rate\"`, which confirms that's the intended name.\n\n**Suggested fix (not applied):**\n1. In `settings.json`, rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`.\n2. Optionally, remove the `except KeyError` fallback in `main.py` so a missing or misspelled setting raises an error instead of printing 0.\n\nShould I apply these changes?\n[tool: grep]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\nThree places read the setting: `main.py`, `billing/report.py` and `billing/export/csv_writer.py`. The cause is the misspelled key in `settings.json`, so I'll fix it there.\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nYes, two other files read the setting. I renamed the misspelled key in `settings.json` from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`, and all three code paths now give the right result.\n\n**Every place that reads `fee_rate`:**\n\n| File:line | How it reads it | Before the fix | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, with a fallback to 0 at lines 12\u201313 | `Total: 0` (wrong, no error) | `Total: 5.0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` | stopped with \"fee_rate is missing\" | `Report fee: 0.5` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`, built from two pieces so a plain text search misses it | stopped with \"fee_rate is missing\" | `CSV fee: 0.5` |\n\nThe shown outputs are from running all three after the change. `app/config.py:15` (`get_setting`) is just the helper that looks the value up.\n\nThese files mention \"fee_rate\" but don't read the setting:\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` is a column name that its comment says is unused.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has its own fixed value, `archived_fee_rate = 0.15`.\n- The comments in `billing/tax.py` and `billing/audit.py` say they aren't the settings key.\n\nI didn't change the `except KeyError: rate = 0` in `main.py:12-13`. It means a missing setting still prints `Total: 0` without any error, while the other two files stop with a clear message. Should I make `main.py` stop with an error the same way?", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 111065, "requests_cache_write": 34751, "requests_cost_usd": 0.28549599999999997, "requests_count": 13, "requests_input_uncached": 1537, "requests_output": 4169, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial7", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 24, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T04:29:32.098973+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 1, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 47.932, "t_checker_s": 0.224, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 5706, "tokens_cache_read": 111065, "tokens_cache_write": 34751, "tokens_fresh": 2664, "tokens_input_uncached": 1537, "tokens_main_cache_read": 81176, "tokens_main_cache_write": 21282, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 2648, "tokens_output": 4169, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 111065, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 34751, "tokens_proxy_calls": 13, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1537, "tokens_proxy_output": 4169, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "